      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge rapids at the clearance plane against the stock\n\nThe mill column law (d) stood down for every lateral rapid at or above\nthe clearance plane. A plane set inside the stock (a Fixed height, or a\nmodel-based one under the stock top) sent the traverse through uncut\nstock and the program posted with no warning.\n\n- sim: the clearance gate is gone. Every lateral rapid under the stock\n  top is marched against the column.\n- sim: two re-reads for the convictions this adds (a lateral rapid at\n  or above the plane), each only removing a conviction:\n  `acquit_traverses_by_solids` (the tool stack against the stock and\n  part solids under the swept strip; the column is capped at the\n  stock's highest point, a 3+2 plane's at the tilted block's highest\n  corner) and `acquit_traverses_by_prior` (the stock the program ahead\n  left, plus the part's facets). A rapid under the plane keeps the old\n  rule: its lateral conviction is never re-read by the prior.\n- app: generate wires both and adds the note \"Clearance in stock:\n  rapid move N travels through stock at Z ...\".\n- app: `operation::clearance_in_stock_advice` names a plane under the\n  top of raw stock when an operation is made or edited; MCP's\n  add_operation and edit_operation answer with it as `warning`.\n- The warning's sentence now reads \"rapid move N travels through stock\n  (below the clearance plane, or at it below the stock top)\"; the\n  troubleshooting page follows.\n\nThe radial, rotary and turning (meridian) rapid laws never had a\nclearance gate and are unchanged. No golden changed.\n\nFixes #2121\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
